=== p2-windows · W7 · page:vehicle-systems/ClimateControl (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:vehicle-systems/ClimateControl   kind=page   web route=/climate
Web source  : web/src/features/vehicle-systems/pages/ClimateControlPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  parsing, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the IXxxFeed data port + Empty + generated-client feed),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable observable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent
  view, a UserControl). The generated prompt's idealized "ClimateControlPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under
  TeslaSync/Features/VehicleSystems" is mapped onto these real conventions. The surface registers with the W4
  ShellPageFactory under route name "ClimateControl" (RouteTable already declares Page("ClimateControl",
  "climate-control") + Hidden("ClimateControl", "climate")).
- Three data sources, each bound through the generated C# client (ADR-004) on the ClimateClientFeed:
  GET /climate/latest (web useClimate, Operations.Climate.Latest), GET /climate (web useClimateHistory, the new
  Operations.Climate.History = get_api_v1_climate) and GET /charging-telemetry/latest (web
  useChargingTelemetryLatest, Operations.Charging.TelemetryLatest, read only for the not-enough-power-to-heat
  banner). Field names are the snake_case wire names the Go climate handler projects
  (internal/api/climate/handler.go: inside_temp, outside_temp, driver_temp_setting, passenger_temp_setting,
  hvac_power, is_ac_on, hvac_auto_mode, fan_speed, hvac_fan_status, climate_keeper_mode, defrost_mode,
  defrost_for_preconditioning, rear_defrost_enabled, wiper_heat_enabled, rear_display_hvac_enabled,
  battery_heater, overheat_protection, cabin_overheat_protection_temp_limit, hvac_steering_wheel_heat_auto,
  hvac_steering_wheel_heat_level, seat_heater_{left,right,rear_left,rear_center,rear_right},
  auto_seat_climate_{left,right}, climate_seat_cooling_front_{left,right}, seat_vent_enabled; history adds id /
  created_at / timestamp; charging adds not_enough_power_to_heat).
- SI units honored: temperatures are SI Celsius on disk and converted to the active unit ONLY at the display
  boundary via the shared P1/S5 ports UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi / UnitFormatters.FormatTemperature /
  UnitLabels.Label (web convertTempFromSI). Gauge max mirrors the web (131 °F / 55 °C). Comfort score and temp
  delta are computed in Celsius exactly as the web memos do.
- i18n: every visible literal flows through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names in the resw
  translation.* catalog form (localizer.GetString("translation.<web phrase>", "<web phrase>")). 55 of the 84
  manifest strings were missing from Strings/en/Resources.resw and were added (plus 11 non-manifest helper
  strings the page also localizes: Low/Medium/Front Left/Front Right/Rear Left/Rear Center/Rear Right/Adjusting/
  Far from target/Dog Mode/Camp Mode); "High" + 28 of the 84 already existed verbatim.
- Charts use the W3 native wrappers only: three TsRadialGauge (Components.Charts), one TsLineChart and one
  TsComposedChart (area AC-state + line fan-speed). No web canvas / recharts. No maps (manifest declares 0).
- Headless test wiring: the three Microsoft.UI-free logic files (.Model.cs/.Source.cs/.ViewModel.cs) are linked
  into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (mirroring every sibling page) so the parser + projection + view-model + feed
  are asserted by ClimateControlPageTests without a UI host.

